---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Schema from '../components/Schema.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from '../components/Breadcrumbs.astro';
import FaqSection from '../components/FaqSection.astro';
import CtaBand from '../components/CtaBand.astro';
import { organizationSchema, faqSchema, breadcrumbSchema, webPageSchema, articleSchema } from '../data/schema';
import { answeringVendors, keresRow, VENDORS_CHECKED } from '../data/answeringVendors';
import { COST_ASSUMPTIONS, costExamplesSorted, monthlyCost, costWorking, usd } from '../data/costExamples';
import { comparisons, ROUNDUP_SLUGS } from '../data/comparisons';

const path = '/ai-receptionist-cost';
const title = 'How Much Does an AI Receptionist Cost? (2026) | Keres AI';
const h1 = 'How Much Does an AI Receptionist Cost? 2026 Prices Compared';
const description = 'AI receptionist prices for 2026, taken from each vendor’s own pricing page: entry plans from $24.95 a month, how billing works, and what 100 calls cost.';
const crumbs = [
  { name: 'Home', path: '/' },
  { name: 'Compare', path: '/compare' },
  { name: 'AI receptionist cost', path },
];

// BLS Occupational Employment and Wage Statistics, May 2025, SOC 43-4171
// (Receptionists and Information Clerks), national median. Read from the BLS
// public API on October 11, 2026 (series OEUN000000000000043417113 and …08).
const BLS = {
  year: 'May 2025',
  medianAnnual: 38010,
  medianHourly: 18.27,
  url: 'https://www.bls.gov/oes/current/oes434171.htm',
};

const vendors = Object.values(answeringVendors);
const roundups = ROUNDUP_SLUGS.map((s) => comparisons.find((c) => c.slug === s)!).filter(Boolean);
const minutes = COST_ASSUMPTIONS.calls * COST_ASSUMPTIONS.avgMinutes;
const ex = costExamplesSorted;
const aiEx = ex.filter((e) => e.type === 'AI');
const liveEx = ex.filter((e) => e.type !== 'AI');

const faqs = [
  { q: 'How much does an AI receptionist cost per month?', a: 'As of October 11, 2026, published entry plans run from $24.95 a month (Upfirst, 30 calls) to $99 a month (My AI Front Desk, 200 voice minutes), and Smith.ai’s AI receptionist has a free tier of 25 calls a month. What you actually pay depends on your call volume and on whether the plan counts minutes, calls or callers.' },
  { q: 'Is per-minute or per-call billing cheaper?', a: 'Per-minute billing is cheaper when calls are short. Per-call billing is cheaper when calls are long, because a ten-minute call costs the same as a one-minute call. Per-caller billing, which Goodcall uses, is cheaper when the same people call several times a month.' },
  { q: 'What is the cheapest AI receptionist?', a: 'On published prices, Smith.ai’s AI receptionist is free for up to 25 calls a month, then $3 per call. The lowest paid plans are Upfirst at $24.95 for 30 calls and Dialzara at $29 for 60 minutes. At 100 calls a month averaging three minutes from 100 different callers, Goodcall’s $79 Starter plan was the lowest of the plans that publish an overage rate.' },
  { q: 'Is an AI receptionist cheaper than a human receptionist?', a: `In wages alone, yes. The BLS puts the ${BLS.year} national median wage for receptionists and information clerks at ${usd(BLS.medianAnnual)} a year (${usd(BLS.medianHourly)} an hour), before payroll taxes and benefits, for about 40 hours of coverage a week. Published AI plans start under $100 a month. A receptionist also does work an AI receptionist does not, such as greeting visitors.` },
  { q: 'How much does Keres AI charge for Remi?', a: 'Keres AI quotes Remi to your call volume: a monthly rate with included minutes, then per minute, with no per-call fees, month-to-month. Found, which runs your website and Google Business Profile, is from $249 a month ($499 for law firms).' },
  { q: 'Why are Ruby, Rosie and Abby Connect missing from the 100-call example?', a: 'Their pricing pages list an entry plan but not the rate charged past it, so the cost of 100 calls cannot be worked out from published figures. We left them out rather than guess. AnsweringLegal does not publish prices at all.' },
];

const article = articleSchema({
  path,
  headline: h1,
  description,
  datePublished: '2026-10-11',
  dateModified: '2026-10-11',
  readingTime: 'PT7M',
});

const webpage = webPageSchema({
  path,
  name: title,
  description,
  speakableSelectors: ['.answer-block', '.faq-a'],
});
---
<Layout title={title} description={description} path={path} ogType="article">
  <Schema slot="head" graph={[article, webpage, faqSchema(faqs), breadcrumbSchema(crumbs), organizationSchema]} />

  <Breadcrumbs crumbs={crumbs} />

  <header class="page-hero container">
    <span class="eyebrow">Pricing · 2026</span>
    <h1>How much does an AI receptionist cost? <span class="accent">2026 prices compared</span></h1>
    <p class="updated" style="font-size:14px;color:var(--text-dim);margin:-8px 0 16px">Updated <time datetime="2026-10-11">October 11, 2026</time> · Written by Keres AI, which sells an AI receptionist (Remi)</p>
    <p class="lead">What AI receptionists and live answering services charge, taken from each vendor’s own pricing page, with the arithmetic for a typical month shown in full.</p>
    <div class="hero-ctas">
      <a href="/quote" class="btn btn-primary">Get a quote for Remi</a>
      <a href="/best-ai-receptionist" class="btn btn-outline">Best AI receptionists</a>
    </div>
  </header>

  <section class="page-section container">
    <div class="answer-block">
      <p>AI receptionists publish entry plans from about $25 to $100 a month in 2026: Upfirst $24.95 for 30 calls, Dialzara $29 for 60 minutes, Rosie $49 for 250 minutes, Goodcall $79 for 100 callers and My AI Front Desk $99 for 200 minutes. Live answering services start higher: Ruby at $250 for 50 minutes, Smith.ai at $300 for 30 calls. Keres AI quotes Remi to your call volume.</p>
      <p style="margin-top:12px;font-size:14px;color:var(--text-dim)">Source: each vendor’s pricing page, checked {VENDORS_CHECKED}.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="page-section container" aria-labelledby="table-title">
    <div class="section-label">Published prices</div>
    <h2 id="table-title" class="section-title" style="margin-bottom:8px">How much does an AI receptionist cost per month?</h2>
    <div class="compare-wrap">
      <table class="compare-table">
        <thead>
          <tr><th>Vendor</th><th>Who answers</th><th>How it bills</th><th>Lowest published plan</th><th>Source</th></tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          {vendors.map((v) => (
            <tr>
              <td>{v.name}</td><td>{v.type}</td><td>{v.billing}</td><td>{v.starting}</td>
              <td><a href={v.source} rel="noopener nofollow" target="_blank">Pricing page</a></td>
            </tr>
          ))}
          <tr class="keres">
            <td><a href={keresRow.url}>{keresRow.name}</a> <em>(that’s us)</em></td>
            <td>{keresRow.type}</td><td>{keresRow.billing}</td><td>{keresRow.starting}</td>
            <td><a href="/pricing">Pricing page</a></td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <p class="prose" style="margin-top:6px">“Hybrid” means people and AI answer on the same line. Prices are the lowest published plan on {VENDORS_CHECKED}, before taxes and any annual-billing discount. They change often; check the vendor’s page before you buy.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="page-section container">
    <div class="prose">
      <h2>How do AI receptionists bill: per minute, per call or per caller?</h2>
      <p><strong>Included minutes, then per minute.</strong> Dialzara, PATLive and Keres AI charge a monthly fee that covers a set number of minutes, then a rate for each extra minute. Ruby, Rosie, Abby Connect and My AI Front Desk also sell plans with included minutes. This suits businesses with short calls, such as booking a service visit or confirming hours, because a quick call uses little of the allowance.</p>
      <p><strong>Per call.</strong> Smith.ai and Upfirst count calls, not minutes: plans include a number of calls, then a rate per extra call. This suits businesses with long calls, such as legal intake or detailed quotes, because a ten-minute call costs the same as a one-minute call.</p>
      <p><strong>Per caller.</strong> Goodcall counts unique phone numbers each month, so a customer who calls five times counts once. This suits businesses whose regular customers call back often, for example to reschedule or check on a job.</p>
      <p><strong>Flat plans with an allowance.</strong> Most plans, whatever they count, are a flat monthly fee with an allowance. The entry price only tells you what a light month costs; the overage rate decides what a busy month costs, so check both.</p>

      <h2>What do 100 calls a month cost?</h2>
      <p>Assumptions: <strong>{COST_ASSUMPTIONS.calls} calls a month, averaging {COST_ASSUMPTIONS.avgMinutes} minutes ({minutes} minutes in total), each from a different caller.</strong> Each figure uses the vendor’s lowest published plan plus its published overage rate, and nothing else.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="compare-wrap">
      <table class="compare-table">
        <thead>
          <tr><th>Vendor</th><th>Who answers</th><th>Plan</th><th>Working</th><th>Monthly cost</th></tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          {ex.map((e) => (
            <tr>
              <td><a href={e.source} rel="noopener nofollow" target="_blank">{e.vendor}</a></td>
              <td>{e.type}</td>
              <td>{e.plan}</td>
              <td>{costWorking(e)}{e.note ? <><br /><small>{e.note}</small></> : null}</td>
              <td><strong>{usd(monthlyCost(e))}</strong></td>
            </tr>
          ))}
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <div class="prose">
      <p><strong>Higher tiers lower the unit rate.</strong> These figures use each vendor’s entry plan. At 100 calls a month, a larger plan from the same vendor can cost less than the entry plan plus overage, so check the vendor’s page for the tier that fits your volume.</p>
      <p><strong>Left out:</strong> Ruby, Rosie and Abby Connect, whose pricing pages do not publish a rate past the plan; AnsweringLegal, which does not publish prices; and Keres AI, which quotes Remi to your volume. Change the assumptions and the order changes: see the worked example on the <a href="/goodcall-alternative">Goodcall alternatives</a> page for repeat callers and one-minute calls.</p>

      <h2>Is an AI receptionist cheaper than an answering service?</h2>
      <p>On published prices, usually yes. In the 100-call example, the AI plans come to {usd(monthlyCost(aiEx[0]))} to {usd(monthlyCost(aiEx[aiEx.length - 1]))} a month, while the live plans that publish overage rates come to {liveEx.map((e) => `${usd(monthlyCost(e))} (${e.vendor.replace(/ \((.*)\)$/, ' $1')})`).join(' and ')}. Entry prices tell the same story: paid AI plans start at $24.95, live plans at $99 (PATLive, 50 minutes) to $300 (Smith.ai, 30 calls).</p>
      <p>What you get differs. A live service puts a person on the call, which helps with upset callers, unusual requests and callers who refuse to talk to AI. An AI receptionist follows your script the same way on every call and can book into your calendar during the call. If a human on every call matters to you, the price gap is the cost of that. Compare live, hybrid and AI options on the <a href="/best-ai-receptionist">best AI receptionists</a> page.</p>

      <h2>Is an AI receptionist cheaper than hiring a receptionist?</h2>
      <p>The U.S. Bureau of Labor Statistics puts the national median wage for receptionists and information clerks (SOC 43-4171) at <strong>{usd(BLS.medianAnnual)} a year, or {usd(BLS.medianHourly)} an hour</strong>, in its {BLS.year} Occupational Employment and Wage Statistics (<a href={BLS.url} rel="noopener" target="_blank">BLS OEWS, 43-4171</a>). That is about {usd(Math.round(BLS.medianAnnual / 12))} a month in wages alone, before payroll taxes, benefits and paid time off, for roughly 40 of the week’s 168 hours.</p>
      <p>Published AI receptionist plans start under $100 a month and answer around the clock. But a receptionist does more than answer the phone: greeting visitors, handling paperwork, and judgment calls an AI should not make. For many small businesses the choice is not either-or; an AI receptionist covers after-hours, overflow and lunch breaks while staff handle the front desk.</p>

      <h2>How does Keres AI price Remi?</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>A monthly rate with included minutes</strong>, quoted to your call volume.</li>
        <li><strong>Per minute after the included minutes</strong>, at the rate in your quote.</li>
        <li><strong>No per-call fees</strong>. Your quote sizes the included minutes to your busy season.</li>
        <li><strong>Month-to-month</strong>, with no long contract.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>Keres AI also sells Found, which builds and runs your website and Google Business Profile and asks customers for reviews, from $249 a month ($499 for law firms). See <a href="/pricing">pricing</a>, <a href="/agents/inbound">how Remi works</a>, or <a href="/hear-it">hear Remi answer a call</a>.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <FaqSection faqs={faqs} title="AI receptionist cost FAQ" />

  <section class="page-section container" aria-labelledby="related-title">
    <div class="section-label">Keep comparing</div>
    <h2 id="related-title" class="section-title" style="margin-bottom:8px">Related comparisons</h2>
    <ul class="prose">
      <li><a href="/best-ai-receptionist">Best AI receptionists for small businesses (2026)</a></li>
      {roundups.map((r) => <li><a href={`/${r.slug}`}>{r.detail?.linkLabel ?? `${r.competitor} alternatives`}</a></li>)}
      <li><a href="/compare">All comparisons</a></li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <CtaBand
    heading="Get Remi quoted to your call volume"
    sub="Tell us roughly how many calls you get and how long they run. We will quote the monthly rate, the included minutes and the per-minute rate after."
  />
</Layout>
